@startuml Composite-BOM-Solution
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title THE SOLUTION — bill of materials WITH Composite\n(package dev.kaldiroglu.composite.bom.solution)\nCost, weight and part counts answered identically for a part and a product

abstract class BomComponent {
  - partNumber : String
  - name : String
  + {abstract} totalCost() : Money
  + {abstract} totalWeightGrams() : int
  + {abstract} partCount() : int
  + lines() : List<BomLine>
  + isAssembly() : boolean
  + toTree() : String
  ~ containsDeep(target) : boolean
}
note right of BomComponent
  Component

  Only QUERIES live here.
  add / remove are declared on
  Assembly — the safe variant of
  GoF p. 168, chosen because the
  many read-only clients never
  edit the structure.
end note

class Part {
  - unitCost : Money
  - weightGrams : int
  + totalCost() : Money
  + totalWeightGrams() : int
  + partCount() : int
}
note bottom of Part
  Leaf

  A purchased part.
  The recursion stops here.
end note

class Assembly {
  - assemblyCost : Money
  - assemblyWeightGrams : int
  - lines : List<BomLine>
  - parents : List<Assembly>
  - cachedCost : Money
  - cachedWeightGrams : Integer
  - cachedPartCount : Integer
  + add(c : BomComponent, qty : int) : Assembly
  + remove(c : BomComponent) : boolean
  + changeQuantity(c : BomComponent, qty : int) : void
  + totalCost() : Money
  + totalWeightGrams() : int
  + partCount() : int
  + parents() : List<Assembly>
  - invalidate() : void
}
note bottom of Assembly
  Composite

  totalCost() = assemblyCost
             + Σ line.extendedCost()

  Caches the roll-up (GoF p. 169) and
  therefore needs parent references
  (GoF p. 167) to invalidate upwards.
end note

class Service {
  - fee : Money
  + totalCost() : Money
  + totalWeightGrams() : int
  + partCount() : int
}
note bottom of Service
  Leaf, added LAST

  A subcontracted operation:
  a fee, 0 g, 0 parts.

  Writing this class was the
  whole change. No client and
  no other class was edited
  (GoF p. 166, consequence 3).
end note

class BomLine <<record>> {
  + component : BomComponent
  + quantity : int
  + extendedCost() : Money
  + extendedWeightGrams() : int
  + extendedPartCount() : int
}
note left of BomLine
  The quantity lives on the EDGE,
  so one sub-assembly object can be
  shared by many parents (GoF p. 167).
end note

class Money <<record>> {
  - amount : BigDecimal
  + plus(other : Money) : Money
  + times(quantity : int) : Money
}

class Main
note top of Main : Client\n(costing, shipping, reporting)

Main --> BomComponent
BomComponent <|-- Part
BomComponent <|-- Service
BomComponent <|-- Assembly
Assembly *--> "lines\n*" BomLine
BomLine --> "1" BomComponent
Assembly ..> "parents\n*" Assembly : invalidates
BomComponent ..> Money

@enduml
